From 0b67df0949d6bbb456a32643b459a84e7ff4cf24 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nuubOS Project <nuubos@localhost>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:45:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] video: add a Wayland platform for V4L2 request hardware
 decoders

Decodes H.264/HEVC with FFmpeg's V4L2 request API hwaccel (Allwinner
Cedrus and other stateless VPUs) and presents the DRM PRIME frames with
zero copies: each capture dma-buf is wrapped once in a linux-dmabuf
wl_buffer and attached to a desynchronized subsurface, fitted with
wp_viewporter over a one-pixel black parent. A frame stays referenced
until the compositor releases its buffer. Frames are shown as soon as
they are decoded; a frame is skipped when newer ones are already queued.
Selected by -platform wayland, or by auto when WAYLAND_DISPLAY is set.
