+/*
+ * Wayland platform for stateless V4L2 decoders (Allwinner Cedrus, Hantro,
+ * rkvdec...), written for nuubOS on the Allwinner H700.
+ *
+ * Decoding: FFmpeg's h264/hevc decoders with the V4L2 request API hwaccel
+ * (AV_HWDEVICE_TYPE_DRM). The VPU writes NV12 straight into V4L2 capture
+ * buffers that FFmpeg exports as dma-bufs (AV_PIX_FMT_DRM_PRIME).
+ *
+ * Presentation: zero copy. Every capture buffer is wrapped once in a
+ * zwp_linux_dmabuf_v1 wl_buffer and attached to a desynchronized
+ * subsurface; the compositor samples it directly. The decoded frame is
+ * referenced until the compositor releases its wl_buffer, so the decoder
+ * never overwrites a buffer on screen. The parent surface is one black
+ * pixel stretched with wp_viewporter (letterbox), the video is fitted with
+ * wp_viewporter too: no scaling or colour conversion on the CPU, no GL
+ * context in this process.
+ *
+ * Latency: frames are presented as soon as they are decoded (the newest
+ * committed buffer wins at the next vblank); when more frames are already
+ * queued, a decoded frame is not presented so a burst after a network
+ * hiccup is caught up instead of being displayed late.
+ *
+ * Wayland events (configure, ping, buffer release) are dispatched by a
+ * dedicated thread that sleeps in poll() without timeout.
+ */
+
